---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../../layouts/layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/footer.astro';
import TokenScope from '../../components/token-scope.astro';
import AgentTopology from '../../components/agent-topology.astro';
import AgentReach from '../../components/agent-reach.astro';
import GuideToc from '../../components/guide-toc.astro';
import { groupByTask } from '../../domain/recipe';

const SIGNUP_URL = 'https://go.marginapp.in';
const TOKENS_URL = 'https://go.marginapp.in/settings';
const LLMS_URL = 'https://go.marginapp.in/llms.txt';

const groups = groupByTask(await getCollection('recipe'));

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'how-it-fits', text: 'How the pieces fit' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'reach', text: 'What an agent can pull together' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'rules', text: 'The rules the recipes share' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'scope', text: 'What a token can reach' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'recipes', text: 'The recipes' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'getting-started', text: 'Getting started' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'trust', text: 'A word on trust' },
];

const rules = [
  {
    title: 'Margin does every computation',
    body: 'Every derived figure comes from the server. An agent that works out its own EPS or intrinsic value produces a saved valuation that disagrees with what the app shows you, and nothing flags the disagreement.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Nothing writes without your go-ahead',
    body: 'Reads are free and repeatable, so a skill can explore as much as it likes. Every write is shown as a diff first and waits for you to say go ahead.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The contract is fetched, never remembered',
    body: 'Margin publishes its own API guide for agents. A skill reads it at the start of every run, because a skill carrying its own copy of the endpoints breaks in hard-to-spot ways when the contract moves.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Your credentials stay on your machine',
    body: 'Your agent talks to your broker and to Margin separately, from where you run it. Margin never sees your broker login in any of this.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Agent recipes · Margin"
  description="Margin publishes an API and a machine-readable guide for AI agents, so you can hand the repetitive parts of portfolio bookkeeping and valuation to a skill you write once. Worked recipes to start from."
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="pt-32 pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[14rem_minmax(0,48rem)] lg:gap-16 lg:justify-center">

      <aside class="hidden lg:block">
        <GuideToc headings={headings} />
      </aside>

      <div class="min-w-0">

      <div class="reveal mb-16">
        <p class="text-xs text-gold-400 tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">Agents</p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-5xl md:text-6xl font-light text-cream leading-tight mb-6">
          Hand the repetitive part<br />
          <em class="font-semibold not-italic">to an agent</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-muted text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-6">
          Keeping a portfolio record honest takes a surprising amount of clerical work. Holdings go
          stale the week you buy something, a year of dividends sits in a console export until you
          remember to fetch it, and the valuation you spent an evening on stays in a spreadsheet
          because retyping it into anything else costs another hour.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          None of that work needs your judgement, only your credentials, a few rules about what
          replaces what, and the patience to check the result. Margin publishes an API
          and a machine-readable guide written for AI agents, so you can write those steps down
          once as a skill and run it whenever you want.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal reveal-delay-1 mb-20">
        <div class="relative rounded-xl border border-border bg-navy-800/40 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-gold-400/30 to-transparent"></div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-3 border-b border-border">
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-navy-600"></span>
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-navy-600"></span>
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-navy-600"></span>
            <span class="ml-2 text-xs text-muted">agent · session</span>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed">
            <p class="text-muted mb-1"># reads the contract, then your two accounts</p>
            <p class="text-gold-300 mb-4">{LLMS_URL}</p>
            <p class="text-muted mb-4">142 holdings at the broker, 139 on record in Margin</p>
            <div class="rounded-lg bg-navy-950/60 border border-amber-400/20 p-4 flex items-start gap-3 mb-2">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-400 mt-1 shrink-0"></span>
              <span class="text-muted">
                2 stocks added, 1 sold out, 4 quantities moved. Write them under
                <span class="text-cream">Zerodha</span>, replacing what is there?
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-lg bg-navy-950/60 border border-emerald-400/20 p-4 flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 mt-1 shrink-0"></span>
              <span class="text-cream">Imported. Read back and matched on ISIN, 142 of 142.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section id="how-it-fits" class="reveal reveal-delay-2 mb-20 scroll-mt-28">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-light text-cream mb-4 gold-line">
          How the pieces fit
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-10">
          The agent runs on your machine, on whatever subscription you already pay for, with only
          the file system, browser and web access you choose to give it. It reaches your broker
          with a login it holds there and Margin with a token it holds there, and the two never
          meet. Margin keeps your data and does every computation. The web app is where you sign
          in to see the same figures and to do the few things a token is not allowed to.
        </p>
        <AgentTopology />
      </section>

      <section id="reach" class="reveal mb-20 scroll-mt-28">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-light text-cream mb-4 gold-line">
          What an agent can pull together
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-10">
          Each source you rely on holds one piece of the picture and none of them can see the
          others. An agent can hold all of them open in the same session, so the workflow becomes
          yours to compose: pull from two or three of them and leave the result where you will look
          for it again. Margin is one of those sources, and the only one that knows what you own,
          what you paid and what you think each company is worth.
        </p>
        <AgentReach />
      </section>

      <section id="rules" class="reveal mb-20 scroll-mt-28">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-light text-cream mb-8 gold-line">
          The rules the recipes share
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
          {rules.map((rule) => (
            <div class="bg-navy-800/30 border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
              <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-cream mb-3 leading-snug">{rule.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">{rule.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="scope" class="reveal mb-20 scroll-mt-28">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-light text-cream mb-4 gold-line">
          What a token can reach
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-8">
          An API token is deliberately narrower than your own login. It can read the summaries a
          skill needs to verify its own work and write the records you hand it, and the operations
          that would lose data or expose the detail of your ledger are reserved for you in the app.
        </p>
        <TokenScope />
      </section>

      <section id="recipes" class="reveal mb-16 scroll-mt-28">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-light text-cream mb-4 gold-line">
          The recipes
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-10">
          Each one explains what the job is, which calls it makes, and what specifically goes
          wrong when you get a detail slightly wrong. Each ends with a skill you can copy into
          your own project and adapt. They are written to be read and changed, not run unaltered,
          because your broker, your accounts and your own tolerance for a script writing to them
          are all yours to set.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-14">
          {groups.map((group) => (
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xs text-gold-400 tracking-widest uppercase mb-5">{group.task}</h3>
              <div class="space-y-4">
                {group.items.map((recipe) => (
                  <article class="group">
                    <a href={`/agents/${recipe.slug}`} class="block bg-navy-800/30 border border-border hover:border-gold-400/30 rounded-xl p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-navy-800/50">
                      <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
                        <div>
                          <h4 class="font-display text-xl font-light text-cream group-hover:text-gold-200 transition-colors duration-200 mb-2 leading-snug">
                            {recipe.data.title}
                          </h4>
                          <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
                            {recipe.data.description}
                          </p>
                          <p class="flex items-start gap-2 text-xs text-muted/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-amber-400/70 mt-px shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m16.862 4.487 1.687-1.688a1.875 1.875 0 1 1 2.652 2.652L10.582 16.07a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-1.897 1.13L6 18l.8-2.685a4.5 4.5 0 0 1 1.13-1.897l8.932-8.931Z" />
                            </svg>
                            Writes: {recipe.data.writes}
                          </p>
                          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
                            {recipe.data.connects.map((system) => (
                              <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[11px] text-muted border border-border rounded-full">{system}</span>
                            ))}
                            {recipe.data.readingTime && (
                              <span class="text-[11px] text-muted/60">{recipe.data.readingTime}</span>
                            )}
                          </div>
                        </div>
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gold-400 shrink-0 mt-1 group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M17.25 8.25L21 12m0 0l-3.75 3.75M21 12H3" />
                        </svg>
                      </div>
                    </a>
                  </article>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="getting-started" class="reveal mb-16 scroll-mt-28">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-light text-cream mb-6 gold-line">
          Getting started
        </h2>
        <ol class="space-y-4 text-muted leading-relaxed list-decimal pl-5 marker:text-gold-400">
          <li>
            Create a token in Margin at <a href={TOKENS_URL} class="text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors">Settings</a>,
            on the API Tokens tab. It starts with <code class="text-gold-300">mgn_</code>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Save it somewhere private on your own machine, readable only by you, and have your
            skills read it from there instead of pasting it into a prompt.
          </li>
          <li>
            Point your agent at <a href={LLMS_URL} class="text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors">go.marginapp.in/llms.txt</a>.
            It covers every operation a token can perform, including the ones no recipe here uses.
          </li>
          <li>
            Pick the recipe closest to the job you keep doing by hand, and start with its read
            steps only. Add the write once you trust what the read shows you.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <div id="trust" class="reveal bg-navy-800/30 border border-gold-400/20 rounded-xl p-8 scroll-mt-28">
        <p class="text-xs text-gold-400 tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">A word on trust</p>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
          These recipes hand a program your broker session and a token that writes to your
          portfolio. Read a skill before you run it, the same way you would read any script that
          touches your accounts. The ones here ask for your go-ahead before every write and show
          you the diff first, and a skill you adapt should keep doing both.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Margin never sees your broker credentials in any of this. Your agent talks to your
          broker and to Margin separately, on your machine, with credentials you hold.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal mt-16 text-center">
        <a
          href={SIGNUP_URL}
          class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-navy-900 bg-gold-400 hover:bg-gold-300 rounded transition-colors duration-200 tracking-wide"
        >
          Create an API token
        </a>
      </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
